{
  "id": 9,
  "title": "IPv4 Addressing Deep Dive",
  "topic": "IPv4 Unicast / Multicast / Broadcast",
  "description": "Three departments share a router. Each has its own /26 subnet carved from 192.168.50.0/24. Assign the correct first-usable IP to each router sub-interface and verify all three department PCs can ping the router gateway.",
  "ccnaRef": "CCNA ITN: Modules 11–12 – IPv4 Addressing",
  "sandboxMode": false,
  "objectives": [
    { "id": "obj1", "desc": "Dept-A PC can ping its gateway (192.168.50.1)" },
    { "id": "obj2", "desc": "Dept-B PC can ping its gateway (192.168.50.65)" },
    { "id": "obj3", "desc": "Dept-C PC can ping its gateway (192.168.50.129)" },
    { "id": "obj4", "desc": "R1 G0/0 is in 192.168.50.0/26" },
    { "id": "obj5", "desc": "R1 G0/1 is in 192.168.50.64/26" },
    { "id": "obj6", "desc": "R1 G0/2 is in 192.168.50.128/26" }
  ],
  "requirements": [
    { "id": "obj1", "type": "ping", "desc": "Dept-A → gateway", "srcDeviceId": "pc-9a", "dstIp": "192.168.50.1" },
    { "id": "obj2", "type": "ping", "desc": "Dept-B → gateway", "srcDeviceId": "pc-9b", "dstIp": "192.168.50.65" },
    { "id": "obj3", "type": "ping", "desc": "Dept-C → gateway", "srcDeviceId": "pc-9c", "dstIp": "192.168.50.129" },
    { "id": "obj4", "type": "subnet", "desc": "R1 G0/0 in .0/26", "hostname": "R1", "interface": "G0/0", "expectedNetwork": "192.168.50.0", "expectedMask": "255.255.255.192" },
    { "id": "obj5", "type": "subnet", "desc": "R1 G0/1 in .64/26", "hostname": "R1", "interface": "G0/1", "expectedNetwork": "192.168.50.64", "expectedMask": "255.255.255.192" },
    { "id": "obj6", "type": "subnet", "desc": "R1 G0/2 in .128/26", "hostname": "R1", "interface": "G0/2", "expectedNetwork": "192.168.50.128", "expectedMask": "255.255.255.192" }
  ],
  "hints": [
    "192.168.50.0/26 gives 4 subnets of 64 IPs each (62 usable hosts). Increment by 64.",
    "Subnet A: 192.168.50.0–63  → gateway 192.168.50.1  mask 255.255.255.192",
    "Subnet B: 192.168.50.64–127 → gateway 192.168.50.65 mask 255.255.255.192",
    "Subnet C: 192.168.50.128–191 → gateway 192.168.50.129 mask 255.255.255.192",
    "Select R1 in the terminal: enable → conf t → int g0/0 → ip address 192.168.50.1 255.255.255.192 → no shut",
    "Repeat for G0/1 and G0/2 with the respective subnet gateways."
  ],
  "topology": {
